1
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,000
This is a bullet casing.

2
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
But I thought anything mechanical
was forbidden here, isn't it?

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,000
It means the underground rulers of the NGL

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
weren't only manufacturing drugs,
but weapons.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000
-Yeah, but judging by this…
-This wasn't a human.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

7
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
[singer singing in English]

8
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

9
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,000
[singer singing in English]

10
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

11
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

12
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:12,000
[narrator] The Chimera Ants continue
their rampage across the NGL

13
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,000
and have finally bared their fangs
at the underground ruler

14
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:19,000
who led this country from the shadows.

15
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:29,000
It's safe for us to assume that
the Chimera Ants have taken full control

16
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,000
of the NGL's interior.

17
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,000
I need much more than this!

18
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:12,000
I require more nutritious food
for this precious child.

19
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:39,000
If the queen commands it, we will gladly
double, or even triple our quota.

20
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:42,000
-Yes, but we must increase our ranks.
-Not so.

21
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,000
after we eliminate sedition
in every last one of--

22
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:59,000
-[Zazan] You've got to be joking!
-[all] Huh?

23
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,000
of a thousand of the normal ones.

24
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:27,000
We're calling them Rares
because they're quite difficult to find.

25
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,000
[Zazan] That's right.

26
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Impossible. No such human could ever--

27
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:41,000
They do exist! Not only did I see one,
but I fought with it, too.

28
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,000
You're lying.

29
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:50,000
The one you took a bite out of
wasn't rare in the least.

30
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,000
Oh, yeah, you're right. I forgot.

31
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:55,000
Stop spouting nonsense.

32
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:58,000
I'm sorry, mistress,
but what you said was nonsense as well.

33
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,000
Well, I was the one who disabled him.

34
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Maybe so.
But I was the one who caught him first.

35
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,000
[whimpers]

36
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,000
That story you told, so was it true?

37
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
[gasps] If it isn't, Lord Bihorn.

38
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:43,000
Of course, it really was a rare human.

39
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:47,000
No, not that.
Did you really take a bite out of it?

40
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:48,000
No. Well, I…

41
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:52,000
I just tasted the normal human,
not the rare one. [grunts]

42
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,000
I will never do it again.

43
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:12,000
Please, spare me just this once,
Lord Bihorn.

44
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Hold it. Come back here at once!

45
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,000
-[Colt] Bihorn.
-[grunts]

46
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:20,000
I'm curious,
have you ever seen a rare human before?

47
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:28,000
Zazan, so this rare human,
can you tell me more about it?

48
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:46,000
Hmm, yes, that must be it.

49
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,000
Well, that does solve one mystery.

50
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,000
It seems the arrows in question,

51
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:55,000
while invisible to the foot soldiers,
can be seen by officers, like Pike.

52
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,000
That means we can stop them.

53
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:00,000
If so, that also means
we can capture them.

54
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:03,000
[Zazan] That's right, just like I did.

55
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:07,000
It was obvious, that one
was very different from the other humans

56
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,000
we've captured so far.

57
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:13,000
In fact, its entire body seemed to be
a shining mass of life energy,

58
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:15,000
and that's how I could tell

59
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:20,000
that Rares have the nutritional value
of over a thousand humans.

60
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:24,000
More than ten days' worth of sustenance
in one human?

61
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:27,000
[Turtle Ant] If that's true,
then we're all saved.

62
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:32,000
That will be significantly easier
than carrying a hundred or so humans

63
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:33,000
around with us every day.

64
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:37,000
Find one on the first day
and we can rest for the next nine.

65
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:41,000
Come on. They're rare because
they're so difficult to find, you idiot.

66
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,000
[Colt] What? Again?

67
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:47,000
-Yes, I understand.
-[Peggy] Is there something wrong?

68
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:52,000
It's about Rammot, it would seem that he's
chosen to act without my permission again.

69
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,000
[Rammot chomping]

70
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:22,000
I know why. It's because of Colt.
This is all his fault.

71
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:41,000
[Colt] I have to deal with Rammot first
before it sets a bad example.

72
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,000
[gasps]

73
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:59,000
This presence, what is it?

74
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,000
[footsteps approaching]

75
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,000
[Gon] Nobody's in here.

76
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:26,000
Hey, something smells bad.

77
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,000
It's coming from over there.

78
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:35,000
-What?
-What the hell is that thing?

79
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:39,000
[Kite] So, they can conceal
their presence.

80
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,000
[growls]

81
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,000
[shudders]

82
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,000
[grunts]

83
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:08,000
[gasps]

84
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
[growls]

85
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,000
[Kite] That's a Chimera Ant soldier.

86
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:34,000
There are bound to be plenty more like him
from here on out.

87
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,000
If you can't defeat him, go home.

88
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:01,000
-I've already told you Kite…
-We're both professionals, too.

89
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:18,000
[Rammot] What trick is this?

90
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:21,000
They seem to have gotten stronger
all of a sudden.

91
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,000
[Rammot yells]

92
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,000
[grunts, groans]

93
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,000
[Rammot screams]

94
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,000
[gasps]

95
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:01,000
[groaning]

96
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:06,000
[Gon] Show me rock!

97
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Janken rock!

98
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:18,000
All right! A perfect shot!

99
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,000
[growls]

100
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:36,000
[roars]

101
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:50,000
I swear on my life,
you're both dead, you hear me?

102
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:58,000
[Gon] Our attacks didn't work.

103
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,000
[Kite] It's because that one's smart.

104
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:07,000
He just let his lackey in to fight,
so that we would tip our hand.

105
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,000
Are you coming?

106
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Hey, don't be so disappointed.

107
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:19,000
Your attacks just now,
they weren't that bad.

108
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:23,000
You just need a bit more experience,
that's all.

109
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:28,000
If you wanna get stronger,
this is a perfect opportunity,

110
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:40,000
From here on out,
in victory or defeat, it'll be hell.

111
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:51,000
-Right, count us in.
-[Killua] Yeah.

112
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,000
[gagging]

113
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:03,000
[straining] God damn it!

114
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:06,000
It hurts! [groaning]

115
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:11,000
Don't you dare lay a finger on them.

116
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:26,000
[Rammot groaning]

117
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:29,000
I'm more than willing
to let you kill them,

118
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,000
but you may not eat them.

119
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:35,000
Bodies brimming with so much life energy
will make prime nourishment.

120
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:38,000
They must be fed to the queen,
you understand that?

121
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:02,000
Ugh! I can't just kill them
and walk away, I can't!

122
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:18,000
The other squads do it all the time,
they told me.

123
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:30,000
-Hold on, is that true?
-Yeah.

124
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:50,000
even if that means
I have to transfer to another unit.

125
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:57,000
[groaning] Damn it, it hurts!

126
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:08,000
That way, you get to know exactly
what they're thinking as they're dying.

127
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:12,000
I do enjoy seeing the fear on their faces.

128
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
It's the best!

129
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:17,000
Once you try it, you never go back.
It's true. [laughs]

130
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:43,000
You shouldn't be wasting the queen's
precious source of nutrition for sport.

131
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:45,000
[Leol chuckles] "Precious"?
Don't make me laugh.

132
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:50,000
Be honest, there are far more of them
than she would ever need.

133
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,000
They're nothing but trash.

134
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:57,000
See, all we're doing is taking out
the garbage. Got a problem with that?

135
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:59,000
[Hina] Of course, not. [giggles]

136
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:03,000
And did you know about the Rares
among the humans?

137
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,000
The Rares, huh?

138
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:10,000
Oh, you must be talking about the ones
that are overflowing with life energy.

139
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:13,000
I still haven't seen one yet myself.

140
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:15,000
If you ever do,

141
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:18,000
you must capture it alive
and bring it back here.

142
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:30,000
Hmm, whatever you say, boss.
I'll offer the rare ones to the queen.

143
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:34,000
Go tell that to Rammot,
maybe that'll get him to calm down.

144
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:57,000
[all laughing]

145
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:23,000
Opinions aren't necessarily a bad thing,
but too many of them are selfish.

146
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:28,000
[Cheetu] We're meeting our quota.
I don't see what there is to worry about.

147
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:32,000
[teases]

148
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Tell me the truth, are you even counting
the humans you capture?

149
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,000
[Cheetu] Mmm, mostly.

150
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:40,000
That isn't helpful.

151
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:46,000
[Peggy] Perhaps we should have everyone
assembled to discuss this.

152
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:49,000
No, we all work different schedules
at the moment.

153
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:51,000
We cannot assemble everyone.

154
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:56,000
Let's talk to them individually
and see if we can come up with a plan.

155
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,000
Fine, but what about the queen?

156
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,000
That's right.

157
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:58,000
further intensifies the ominous air.

158
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:03,000
-[wind whistling]
-But what awaits Gon and his friends?

159
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:10,000
[closing theme music playing]

160
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:22,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

161
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:35,000
[Gon] Next time, "Kite and Slots".

162
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:39,000
Start the slots. Brrr! Beep-beep-beep.

163
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:41,000
Click-click-click. Boom!

164
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:45,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
